The site's m-bootloader from the firmware (tools/make_site.py): fm1.toml mboot = "DIR" (in APP_DIR: fm1-uboot-X.Y.fwsc
and its LICENSE) and mboot_version = "X.Y" make the installer offer that package instead of fm1-base's
(web/m-bootloader/, MBOOT_VERSION 1.2). Without the keys nothing changes. The package is checked for m-bootloader's
identity (FM-1_099), which the installer page asks for too.
Why MIDIMON needs it: fm1-base carries m-bootloader 1.2, which stops at BAD CONFIG with stock V16's boot area (fixed
in 1.3) and after which one FM-1 with the newer UC25HQ80 flash did not start; MIDIMON's installer offers 2.2
(app/site/m-bootloader/README.md). Goes when fm1-base carries 2.2 or newer, or takes the option.
Applies to: fm1-base 317cb86, after 0001-0004. Upstream: not offered yet (a pull request would be this file alone).
